      "writtenOn": "2022-11-09T15:24:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Does it actually have dimensions?\n\nYea, this is perhaps a bit confusing, but my current vision of things is: RenderPassTask has a field fTarget which can represent a special surface as a fully-lazy TextureProxy. But by the time we call RenderPassTask::addCommands, the TextureProxy must be instantiated with an actual surface (accordingly we assert the proxy is instantiated at the beginning of addCommands). So when we call CommandBuffer::addRenderPass, we provide fTarget-\u003edimensions() for the viewport which is valid and reflects the dimensions of the actual surface.\n\n\u003e Maybe we don\u0027t need to have explicit SetViewport commands?\n\nEspecially given the concern about replaying with transforms, I would agree with that.",
      "parentUuid": "6aafc5a5_732b3291",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 65,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 65,
        "endChar": 38
      },
